# Kept out of every build context.
#
# Without this, `docker compose build` on a development machine uploads the
# whole repo including node_modules and every build output - hundreds of
# megabytes, none of it used, and some of it actively wrong: a host-built
# node_modules carries binaries compiled for the host, not for Alpine.
#
# The server builds from a fresh clone where most of this does not exist, so
# this file is mainly what makes building from a working copy behave the same
# way as building on the server.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Every image rebuilds what it needs from source.
dist
**/dist
**/dist-electron
**/dist-web
**/release
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Generated during packaging.
apps/desktop/build

# Published installers. Large, and served from a bind mount rather than baked
# into an image.
updates

# Secrets. Compose passes what a container needs through the environment.
.env
.env.local
.env.production
**/.env.production

.git
.github
.gitignore
.vscode
*.md
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
